s gone:\n- With no selector it now runs a smaller N≤3 version by default. A new always-run test puts the conflicting object at every position among 3 common IDs, with a peer-only record, over 432 cases.\n- A new test fails on any unjustified `t.Skip` in the package, and a planted skip is caught.\n- The `.pyc` build artifact is gone from the tree.\n- Rev5 changes only tests, docs, the mutation harness and the registry. `durable.go` is the same as in rev4.\n\n**Plants on the sync audit loop**, each run with `go test ./internal/merkleinventory` and no selector:\n\n| Plant | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Neutral control | survived, exit 0 |\n| rev4's plant E (audit only the first common ID) | killed |\n| Audit only the last ID | killed |\n| Audit only even positions | killed |\n| Audit only odd positions | killed |\n| Audit only first and last | killed |\n| Audit only the first namespace | killed |\n| Audit only the first ID when the peer holds extra objects | killed |\n\n**Required checks I reran myself on the exact tree:**\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Full `go test ./...` | all ok except `specpin` in the archive copy, which needs `.task-board`; it passes in the live worktree |\n| `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` and gofmt | exit 0, clean |\n| tracecheck and digest | green: 163 acceptance cases, 88/610 clauses discharged, pinned digest still matches |\n| Registry plant | renaming the new test in the registry makes tracecheck fail |\n| README plant | changing the coverage figure to 89/610 fails the README pin test |\n| Importer grid, base vs candidate (27 packages) | no test changed pass/fail. The canonicaljson tombstone/tombstone-ack \"unsupported\" subtests are gone because those schemas are now supported (§10), same as rev4. The tmuxserver subtest changes are only because their names depend on the scratch path length. |\n| Determinism, `-count=3` on the new tests | ok |\n| Shipped mutation harness, run twice | the 12 sync and skip-census rows killed both times, the control survived |\n| `task-board.config.json` | byte-identical to base |\n\nNo findings. There are two non-blocking notes:\n- The AST check on the audit loop only matches identifiers, so the always-on behavioural test is what actually catches the narrowings.\n- The tmuxserver subtest names change with the path length, which is noise in the importer grid and not caused by this Story.\n\nThe verdict (`TASK-260830-2h5uv9_review-verdict-rev5.md`) and the evidence tar (about 590 KB) are attached to the task. I checked the remaining checklist items and deleted the scratch directory.","ttft_ms":1656,"type":"result","duration_ms":2462792,"uuid":"efd47900-a67c-48b4-947a-5e8386a6f26b","ttft_stream_ms":1451,"time_to_request_ms":57,"first_content_frame_ms":1451,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
